No code is shown that prevents `clear()` from being called before or between uses of `Game.world().camera()`. Since the analysis must consider whether this call *can* be null at runtime at this site (not whether it usually is), the fact that `clear()` can legitimately set the camera to null is sufficient to show that:

```java
Game.world().camera()
```

